# Plans a drive from one pose to another through the drivable areas (MowBite Planner, mowbite_planner): to the first
# pose of a coverage path, between its sections, between areas, to the dock. Forwards only.
# Coordinates are metres in a flat frame, the planner's frame_id parameter (default map), poses of base_link.

# where the mower is and the way it faces
geometry_msgs/Pose start
geometry_msgs/Pose goal
# true: arrive facing the goal's orientation. false: any way
bool use_goal_heading false
# m straight on before the goal, facing its way (e.g. to back onto the dock's contacts from there), needs
# use_goal_heading
float64 goal_straight_length 0.0
# where the mower may drive (mowing and navigation areas): at least one, at least 3 points each. The way keeps the
# strictest margins and edges the map's areas with these outlines have (one of no area: the strictest of the map's,
# said in message)
geometry_msgs/Polygon[] drivable_areas
# no-go zones (flower beds, trees)
geometry_msgs/Polygon[] obstacles
# kept out of for this request only (seen by the robot, not in the map): hard lines whatever the map's edges are read
# as, no margin of their own (the robot's clearance in them), the body checked against them like against any edge.
# 16 at most, 3 to 64 points each, each within 3 m of its centre, else BAD_REQUEST
geometry_msgs/Polygon[] temporary_obstacles
# the ones to drive past instead at the start (none: the temporary obstacles only), else one for each of them, in
# their order, smaller (the robot's clearance driving past them): where no way leaves the start with the temporary
# obstacles and the body can't turn round there (stopped right ahead of one), the way turns away on the spot and goes
# straight on with the body out of these, till it's out of the temporary obstacles (said in message); one for each
# or none, else BAD_REQUEST
geometry_msgs/Polygon[] temporary_passing
# m, how far the start or the goal may lie outside of where the body fits (by the edge, the dock), the way from or to
# there runs straight and unchecked. < 0: 0.5, more than 1.0: BAD_REQUEST
float64 max_outside -1.0
# Overrides for this request, any of the node's parameters by its name (e.g. turn_radius, turn_on_spot, robot_width).
# Left out, the node's parameters apply.
rcl_interfaces/Parameter[] overrides
---
bool success
# why planning failed, or a summary and any warnings: to show, not to go by
string message
# empty with success, else why not, to go by:
#   NOT_READY      nothing is planned now (the mower's dimensions not there yet or not usable): ask again later
#   NO_WAY         no way from the start to the goal with the body in
#   START_OUTSIDE  the start lies further outside of where the body fits than max_outside
#   GOAL_OUTSIDE   the goal does
#   BAD_REQUEST    an override the node doesn't take, a value out of range, no drivable area
#   SEARCH_LIMIT   no way found in the node's transit_search_limit s (there may be one)
#   INTERNAL       an error of the planner's own
string code
# The way: each pose faces the next one, the last one the way it arrives, waypoint_spacing apart, at least 3, no two on
# the same position. A pose whose heading jumps from the one before (by more than 15 deg) turns on the spot there.
# Empty where the start is at the goal already: closer than waypoint_spacing, facing its way within 15 deg, or with
# turn_on_spot turning there on the spot into the goal's heading is checked (the body in where the start is and at the
# goal; the driver turns there). Where it isn't, a way like any other, or NO_WAY.
nav_msgs/Path path
# m
float64 path_length
# the poses it turns on the spot at, 0: at the start, from the start's heading into the first pose's
uint32[] spin_at
# m of the way from the start, and before the goal, where the body isn't checked (it lay outside, see max_outside)
float64 start_outside
float64 goal_outside
